at the state parameter can be exotic . this figure is plotted with the same constants used in fig . [ fig : r ] . ] now , the solutions ( [ nc : omega ] ) and ( [ nc : chi ] ) should be satisfied with the constraint ( [ con ] ) , which determines the integration function , . \ ] ] then , the induced energy - momentum tensors ( [ t++ ] ) , and ( [ t+- ] ) are obtained as , \ t_{+-}^{m qt } & = &  rac12  eta \kappa^2	heta^2 e^{\kappa	heta t}. \ ] ] using eqs . ( [ def : energy ] ) and ( [ def : pressure ] ) , the energy density , the pressure are explicitly given as , \ ] ] so that the state parameter reads where its profile is plotted in fig . [ fig : energy ] for the special case giving the ads - ds transition . the energy density and the pressure are the same value of approximately at the initial time corresponding to , and then the state parameter becomes . the energy density becomes zero at the comoving time , where where \ln [ \kappa/(4 eta)]$ ] . it changes from negative value to positive around , but the pressure is always negative . the state parameter diverges at since the energy density vanishes faster than the pressure . the decelerated expansion of the early universe is due to the negative energy density with the negative pressure induced by quantum back reaction , and the accelerated late - time universe comes from the positive energy and the negative pressure which behave like dark energy source . we have shown that the phase changing transition from the ads to the ds phase is possible by assuming the modified poisson brackets to the semiclassical equations of motion in the bpp model . the usual bpp model does not generate this kind of transition since the integration function related to the vacuum state is trivially constant , and the equation of state parameter is simply one which is independent of the time . so , we have taken the nontrivial poisson brackets at the semiclassical level to overcome this triviality . the modified poisson brackets are n